# =============================================================================================
# Circuit — Microsoft Store identity. THE ONE PLACE the Partner Center values get pasted.
#
#   cp windows/msix/partner-center.env.example windows/msix/partner-center.env
#   <edit the three values below>
#   bash windows/build-msix.sh --validate     # confirms all three resolved
#
# partner-center.env is gitignored: it is account identity, not source.
# None of these three values exist until the app name is RESERVED in Partner Center.
# NEVER invent them. A guessed GUID or publisher string fails Store ingestion and, worse,
# looks real in a diff.
#
# SYNTAX: this file is sourced by bash. ALWAYS quote the values — the legal name contains
# spaces, and an unquoted value silently loses everything after the first space.
#     PARTNER_CENTER_PUBLISHER_DISPLAY="Jane Q Public"     <- correct
#     PARTNER_CENTER_PUBLISHER_DISPLAY=Jane Q Public       <- WRONG, resolves to "Jane"
# build-msix.sh prints the resolved values and an IDENTITY-PLACEHOLDER / STORE-READY verdict,
# so run `bash windows/build-msix.sh --validate` and read them back before you trust this file.
#
# Where each value comes from, verbatim, in Partner Center:
#   Partner Center -> Apps and games -> <your app> -> Product identity
# That page shows exactly three fields. They map 1:1 to the three variables here.
# =============================================================================================

# 1. Package/Identity/Name
#    Partner Center calls this "Package/Identity/Name".
#    Shape:  <StoreAssignedPrefix>.Circuit   e.g. 12345ExamplePrefix.Circuit
#    The prefix is assigned; do not invent it.
#    Charset is restricted: letters, digits, '.' and '-' only. No spaces, no underscores.
PARTNER_CENTER_IDENTITY_NAME=""

# 2. Package/Identity/Publisher
#    Partner Center calls this "Package/Identity/Publisher".
#    Looks like:  CN=A1B2C3D4-5E6F-7890-ABCD-EF1234567890
#    It is a GUID Microsoft assigns to the ACCOUNT. Copy it character for character,
#    including the leading "CN=". Do not type a company name here.
PARTNER_CENTER_IDENTITY=""

# 3. Package/Properties/PublisherDisplayName
#    Partner Center calls this "Package/Publisher display name".
#    THIS ACCOUNT IS REGISTERED AS AN INDIVIDUAL, so this is the owner's verified LEGAL NAME
#    exactly as it appears on the Partner Center account — NOT a company or brand name.
#    A mismatch against the verified account name is a hard Store ingestion rejection.
PARTNER_CENTER_PUBLISHER_DISPLAY=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Store package version. Must be 4 parts and the REVISION (4th) must be 0 —
# the Store reserves it. Leave unset to use the manifest's committed 1.0.0.0.
# PARTNER_CENTER_PACKAGE_VERSION="1.0.0.0"
